WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.690
Security testing verifies whether assumptions, controls, and expected behaviors hold under realistic conditions.

2
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:15.302
Unit tests can check security behavior in small pieces of code, such as authorization decisions or validation logic.

3
00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:19.839
Integration tests can confirm that components work together safely.

4
00:00:19.839 --> 00:00:29.144
Abuse-case tests exercise scenarios where a feature might be misused, while regression tests help keep fixed security issues from returning.

5
00:00:29.144 --> 00:00:39.601
Automated techniques include static analysis at a high level, dynamic testing at a high level, dependency scanning, container scanning, and secrets scanning.

6
00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.754
Each method sees a different part of the problem.

7
00:00:42.754 --> 00:00:46.061
Static analysis can identify risky code patterns.

8
00:00:46.061 --> 00:00:49.829
Dynamic testing can observe behavior in a running system.

9
00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:54.673
Dependency and container scanners can find known vulnerable components.

10
00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:58.595
Secrets scanners can catch credentials before they spread.

11
00:00:58.595 --> 00:01:00.133
Testing has limits.

12
00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:05.362
False positives are reported issues that do not apply as described after review.

13
00:01:05.362 --> 00:01:09.130
False negatives are real issues that the test did not find.

14
00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:18.742
Manual security review and penetration testing at a high level can add human judgment, but they still do not replace secure requirements and design.

15
00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:20.818
Testing is evidence, not magic.

16
00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:25.893
It verifies selected assumptions; it does not prove the entire system is safe.

17
00:01:25.893 --> 00:01:32.275
Findings must be triaged, assigned, fixed, validated, and tracked to closure or risk acceptance.

18
00:01:32.275 --> 00:01:34.967
A report that nobody owns is not a control.

19
00:01:34.967 --> 00:01:44.502
Teams need severity criteria, service-level expectations, retest steps, and a way to distinguish urgent defects from lower-risk improvements.

20
00:01:44.502 --> 00:01:50.115
The secure SDLC turns testing output into engineering work that improves the product.
